1
00:02:26,687 --> 00:02:28,773
Previously on Dating Alys Perez.

2
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:31,036
Is it about the cousins?

3
00:02:31,036 --> 00:02:33,038
Are you sure Alys is happy with you?

4
00:02:33,163 --> 00:02:36,958
What do I have to do
to prove that I love you?

5
00:02:36,958 --> 00:02:38,585
And you're the only one I love!

6
00:02:38,585 --> 00:02:39,961
Marry me.

7
00:02:40,086 --> 00:02:41,671
Would you like to know

8
00:02:42,130 --> 00:02:43,882
how she looks at me

9
00:02:43,882 --> 00:02:45,258
even when she's mad at me?

10
00:02:46,092 --> 00:02:47,636
The wedding is in two days.

11
00:02:48,345 --> 00:02:49,596
Marry me,

12
00:02:50,138 --> 00:02:51,473
or lose me forever.

13
00:02:52,682 --> 00:02:54,059
Motherfucker!

14
00:02:54,434 --> 00:02:56,561
- You asshole!
- Alys still loves me.

15
00:02:56,561 --> 00:02:57,896
I can still feel it, Tripp.

16
00:03:01,816 --> 00:03:03,818
Alys, we were both hurt.

17
00:03:03,818 --> 00:03:05,445
Just this once.

18
00:03:05,612 --> 00:03:07,656
Show him that I’m your priority.

19
00:03:28,718 --> 00:03:30,220
It's so good.

20
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:32,097
Alys, that's enough!

21
00:03:32,097 --> 00:03:33,723
Look at yourself, you're drunk!

22
00:03:34,015 --> 00:03:36,601
- Then just leave if you want to!
- Alys, we have to go!

23
00:03:36,601 --> 00:03:39,604
I have an important client
breakfast meeting tomorrow.

24
00:03:41,231 --> 00:03:43,566
So, just leave me already!

25
00:03:43,566 --> 00:03:46,069
Just like how your cousin left me.

26
00:03:47,070 --> 00:03:48,446
I knew it.

27
00:03:49,030 --> 00:03:50,240
That's what this is about.

28
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:52,909
Huh?

29
00:03:52,909 --> 00:03:54,202
What?

30
00:03:54,202 --> 00:03:55,328
Nothing.

31
00:03:55,745 --> 00:03:56,705
Come on.

32
00:03:56,705 --> 00:03:57,552
Let's go.

33
00:03:57,622 --> 00:03:58,498
That's enough.

34
00:03:58,498 --> 00:04:01,042
Just one more round, please!

35
00:04:01,209 --> 00:04:03,086
Alys, I have a meeting tomorrow!

36
00:04:04,379 --> 00:04:06,256
You're such a buzzkill!

37
00:04:06,256 --> 00:04:08,425
Just like your cousin in highschool!

38
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:11,177
Hey!

39
00:04:11,177 --> 00:04:12,512
Where are you going?

40
00:04:12,679 --> 00:04:14,055
Didn't you say we were leaving?

41
00:04:15,724 --> 00:04:16,975
I'm going to the restroom.

42
00:04:16,975 --> 00:04:17,934
Meet me outside.

43
00:04:18,435 --> 00:04:19,144
Are you sure you can?

44
00:04:19,144 --> 00:04:19,602
Yes, I—

45
00:04:19,602 --> 00:04:20,854
Hey, hey!

46
00:04:21,062 --> 00:04:23,231
I said, I can manage!

47
00:04:26,776 --> 00:04:28,236
Have you ordered already, Ma’am?

48
00:04:28,236 --> 00:04:29,779
You can choose from our menu here.

49
00:04:30,447 --> 00:04:31,364
Here you go.

50
00:04:31,364 --> 00:04:34,284
Josh, please take their orders.

51
00:04:37,245 --> 00:04:38,204
Alys!

52
00:04:38,204 --> 00:04:40,206
Alys—
I’m sorry, ma’am, sorry!

53
00:04:40,206 --> 00:04:41,262
Alys!

54
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:42,876
- Erica.
- Yes, Ma’am?

55
00:04:42,876 --> 00:04:43,918
How are we on the deliveries?

56
00:04:43,918 --> 00:04:45,295
Yes, Ma'am. They've arrived.

57
00:04:45,295 --> 00:04:46,504
- Thank you. Please do an inventory check.
- Yes, Ma’am.

58
00:04:46,504 --> 00:04:47,647
Alys! Alys!

59
00:04:47,672 --> 00:04:48,798
Tofer, what?!

60
00:04:48,798 --> 00:04:50,342
So early in the morning!

61
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:51,593
Did you hear?

62
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:53,720
Did you hear?!

63
00:04:53,887 --> 00:04:56,473
I'm not deaf you
don't have to shout!

64
00:04:56,473 --> 00:04:57,349
Did you hear already?

65
00:04:57,349 --> 00:04:59,100
I'm not deaf, okay!

66
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,186
Would you stop
repeating yourself?

67
00:05:01,186 --> 00:05:02,979
I can understand
you just fine!

68
00:05:02,979 --> 00:05:04,814
And why are you so excited?

69
00:05:05,231 --> 00:05:07,359
Does Riri have a concert
here in the Philippines?

70
00:05:07,359 --> 00:05:08,651
Hey, I would love that!

71
00:05:09,027 --> 00:05:10,862
But, I've got better news!

72
00:05:10,862 --> 00:05:12,322
What is it?

73
00:05:12,322 --> 00:05:14,240
Tripp's back!

74
00:07:18,907 --> 00:07:19,970
Alys?

75
00:07:20,283 --> 00:07:21,910
Earth to Alys!

76
00:07:22,827 --> 00:07:24,370
Didn't you hear me?

77
00:07:24,829 --> 00:07:26,080
Tripp is back!

78
00:07:30,502 --> 00:07:31,753
Come on, move!

79
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:36,727
Huh?

80
00:07:37,467 --> 00:07:39,260
Hey, Alys!

81
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:40,887
Calm down, calm down!

82
00:07:41,387 --> 00:07:42,430
Inhale.

83
00:07:43,348 --> 00:07:44,349
Exhale.

84
00:07:44,641 --> 00:07:45,774
One more, one more.

85
00:07:45,808 --> 00:07:46,684
Inhale.

86
00:07:47,602 --> 00:07:48,603
Exhale.

87
00:07:49,479 --> 00:07:50,470
Smells like lunch.

88
00:07:50,688 --> 00:07:51,564
Just kidding.

89
00:07:51,856 --> 00:07:52,749
So?

90
00:07:52,774 --> 00:07:53,556
What?

91
00:07:54,025 --> 00:07:54,943
Are you good now?

92
00:07:55,777 --> 00:07:56,774
Okay.

93
00:07:56,961 --> 00:07:58,379
Listen carefully.

94
00:07:58,404 --> 00:08:00,406
I just came from there, right?

95
00:08:01,066 --> 00:08:02,290
Then out of nowhere,

96
00:08:02,784 --> 00:08:04,327
he showed up!

97
00:08:05,245 --> 00:08:06,287
So, what?

98
00:08:06,287 --> 00:08:07,330
Do you understand?

99
00:08:09,374 --> 00:08:10,708
Apparently not.

100
00:08:12,043 --> 00:08:13,127
But,

101
00:08:13,127 --> 00:08:14,546
what I mean is

102
00:08:15,129 --> 00:08:18,066
you should go see him, now!

103
00:08:18,091 --> 00:08:19,342
Come on, come on!

104
00:08:19,634 --> 00:08:21,469
<i>I want to see him, but...</i>

105
00:08:22,303 --> 00:08:23,596
<i>I'm scared.</i>

106
00:08:24,389 --> 00:08:26,558
<i>What will I say to him?</i>

107
00:08:27,016 --> 00:08:29,852
<i>Hi? Hello? How's New York?</i>

108
00:08:30,436 --> 00:08:31,229
<i>Damn.</i>

109
00:08:31,229 --> 00:08:33,648
<i>For the first time, I didn't </i>
<i>know what to say to Tripp.</i>

110
00:08:34,232 --> 00:08:35,650
Gosh.

111
00:08:35,650 --> 00:08:37,694
Tripp's even more handsome now.

112
00:08:37,986 --> 00:08:39,821
Watch out!

113
00:08:44,659 --> 00:08:45,702
Hey!

114
00:08:46,111 --> 00:08:47,602
Why are you still frozen?

115
00:08:48,079 --> 00:08:49,415
Move, Perez!

116
00:08:54,377 --> 00:08:56,212
Aren't you going to see him?

117
00:08:58,298 --> 00:08:59,556
Maybe tomorrow.

118
00:09:00,086 --> 00:09:00,961
Huh?

119
00:09:01,551 --> 00:09:02,696
But why?

120
00:09:03,344 --> 00:09:05,638
You've waited for him for so long.

121
00:09:06,097 --> 00:09:07,557
And now he’s here!

122
00:09:11,561 --> 00:09:14,016
These things take time, Tofer.

123
00:09:14,439 --> 00:09:16,274
And we'll talk to
each other soon, okay?

124
00:09:18,701 --> 00:09:20,620
Just let me do things the
way I want to do them.

125
00:09:22,188 --> 00:09:23,698
I want to take my time.

126
00:09:26,701 --> 00:09:27,702
Okay, fine.

127
00:09:28,453 --> 00:09:29,579
Whatever you say.

128
00:09:30,955 --> 00:09:32,123
Oh, wait.

129
00:09:32,206 --> 00:09:33,884
Where were you the other night?

130
00:09:34,667 --> 00:09:35,585
You know,

131
00:09:35,585 --> 00:09:37,086
I waited for you outside.

132
00:09:37,378 --> 00:09:38,921
When I came back for you,

133
00:09:38,921 --> 00:09:40,590
you were gone!

134
00:09:41,215 --> 00:09:44,636
I looked for you everywhere.
Even in the ladies' room!

135
00:09:44,927 --> 00:09:46,220
What happened to you?

136
00:10:06,991 --> 00:10:08,451
Drake!

137
00:10:09,744 --> 00:10:11,204
What an asshole!

138
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:14,290
Is this guy for real?!

139
00:10:14,339 --> 00:10:15,668
Wake up!

140
00:10:16,918 --> 00:10:18,127
Wake up, Drake!

141
00:10:21,631 --> 00:10:22,840
Who's Fier?

142
00:10:28,971 --> 00:10:30,848
What's so funny about what I said?

143
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:34,309
Nothing.

144
00:10:34,560 --> 00:10:35,687
Why are you here, Alys?

145
00:10:36,234 --> 00:10:37,360
I asked you first.

146
00:10:38,439 --> 00:10:39,524
Goodbye, Alys.

147
00:10:39,524 --> 00:10:40,496
Drake!

148
00:10:44,779 --> 00:10:45,697
Let go.

149
00:10:48,783 --> 00:10:49,909
Let go, Alys!

150
00:10:56,833 --> 00:10:58,334
Come on, Drake.

151
00:11:00,044 --> 00:11:00,988
Tripp.

152
00:11:01,421 --> 00:11:03,923
You left me for Tripp.

153
00:11:04,215 --> 00:11:05,466
Now, go to him, Alys.

154
00:11:07,009 --> 00:11:08,105
Stop bothering me.

155
00:11:10,012 --> 00:11:11,514
Drake, what the fuck is your deal?!

156
00:11:11,514 --> 00:11:13,015
Alys, what do you mean,
what's my deal?!

157
00:11:15,226 --> 00:11:16,436
Who's Fier?

158
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:19,313
Did you replace me with her?!

159
00:11:19,313 --> 00:11:20,356
You're drunk.

160
00:11:20,668 --> 00:11:21,733
Go home.

161
00:11:24,902 --> 00:11:26,195
Damn you, Palma!

162
00:11:28,448 --> 00:11:29,590
Drake!

163
00:11:31,534 --> 00:11:32,910
Damn it, Drake!

164
00:11:34,704 --> 00:11:35,580
Drake!

165
00:11:39,625 --> 00:11:40,543
Drake!

166
00:11:42,712 --> 00:11:43,629
Drake!

167
00:12:17,285 --> 00:12:18,730
Stop it, Alys.

168
00:12:23,998 --> 00:12:25,035
Alys.

169
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:36,057
Don't be jealous.

170
00:12:37,850 --> 00:12:40,728
I'm sure you know that
I still love you, right?

171
00:12:42,647 --> 00:12:44,090
When I told you that

172
00:12:44,535 --> 00:12:47,105
I love you to the moon and back,

173
00:12:48,319 --> 00:12:51,989
I meant that I'll never love
anyone else after you.

174
00:12:55,844 --> 00:12:57,449
Our love was a great deal.

175
00:12:59,205 --> 00:13:01,465
You've drained every bit of my love.

176
00:13:03,876 --> 00:13:05,253
But that's it.

177
00:13:07,547 --> 00:13:08,923
We had our time.

178
00:13:10,633 --> 00:13:12,385
I'll still love you.

179
00:13:14,387 --> 00:13:15,816
But leave me be.

180
00:13:18,349 --> 00:13:19,767
Don't worry about Fier.

181
00:13:20,810 --> 00:13:22,603
She's nothing compared to you.

182
00:13:28,651 --> 00:13:30,111
I’m setting you free.

183
00:13:31,863 --> 00:13:33,364
So, please let me go as well.

184
00:13:34,991 --> 00:13:37,285
We should let go of each other.

185
00:13:39,203 --> 00:13:40,830
Take care of my cousin.

186
00:13:47,420 --> 00:13:48,546
Best wishes.

187
00:13:49,171 --> 00:13:50,449
[in French] Only you.

188
00:14:25,082 --> 00:14:26,016
Alys!

189
00:14:27,668 --> 00:14:28,294
Come on,

190
00:14:28,294 --> 00:14:29,962
I've been trying to talk to you!

191
00:14:30,087 --> 00:14:31,213
Didn’t you hear what I said?

192
00:14:31,213 --> 00:14:33,507
Is something bothering you?
What's in your head?

193
00:14:33,507 --> 00:14:34,467
- I don't know how—
- Nothing.

194
00:14:34,467 --> 00:14:35,134
Nothing.

195
00:14:35,134 --> 00:14:36,193
Nothing, Tofer.

196
00:14:36,218 --> 00:14:37,227
It's nothing.

197
00:14:41,933 --> 00:14:43,809
- Let's go to Tripp?
- Huh?

198
00:14:45,061 --> 00:14:46,020
Yes.

199
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:47,104
Let's go to Tripp.

200
00:14:47,688 --> 00:14:49,482
Wow, what happened to

201
00:14:49,482 --> 00:14:51,192
let me do things when
I wanna do them?

202
00:14:51,192 --> 00:14:52,735
I wanna take my time.

203
00:14:53,861 --> 00:14:54,737
Hmm?

204
00:14:55,091 --> 00:14:56,843
You're serious about this.

205
00:14:56,906 --> 00:14:58,658
So? Should we go to Tripp?

206
00:15:00,284 --> 00:15:03,305
Great, I'll drive! Let's go, let's go!

207
00:15:06,874 --> 00:15:08,250
Lani,

208
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:09,377
is Tripp home?

209
00:15:09,377 --> 00:15:10,503
He's right outside.

210
00:15:10,753 --> 00:15:11,837
Okay, thank you.

211
00:15:14,726 --> 00:15:16,603
This calls for a drink!

212
00:15:16,943 --> 00:15:17,693
Hang on.

213
00:15:17,718 --> 00:15:19,261
I’ll grab some glasses!

214
00:15:19,261 --> 00:15:20,304
Woo!

215
00:15:20,304 --> 00:15:21,555
Let's party!

216
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:24,558
Your hair looks awful.

217
00:15:24,558 --> 00:15:26,435
You're so annoying!

218
00:15:26,435 --> 00:15:27,937
- I'm kidding!
- You're so mean to me!

219
00:15:28,437 --> 00:15:29,438
Pretty?

220
00:15:29,438 --> 00:15:30,106
Who’s that?

221
00:15:30,106 --> 00:15:30,886
Says who?

222
00:15:32,483 --> 00:15:33,484
They’re probably blind.

223
00:15:33,484 --> 00:15:34,485
- Whatever!
- Hmm?

224
00:15:35,361 --> 00:15:36,404
They probably needed money.

225
00:15:36,404 --> 00:15:37,279
Hey!

226
00:15:37,279 --> 00:15:39,824
Probably had bad eyesight.

227
00:15:40,241 --> 00:15:42,159
They were only saying that
so you'd lend them money.

228
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:45,830
Alys!

229
00:15:46,372 --> 00:15:47,331
Kei?

230
00:15:51,794 --> 00:15:52,628
Come!

231
00:15:52,670 --> 00:15:53,379
Join us.

232
00:16:05,433 --> 00:16:06,225
Hey!

233
00:16:07,059 --> 00:16:07,893
Are you okay?

234
00:16:08,519 --> 00:16:09,311
Yes!

235
00:16:09,311 --> 00:16:10,285
I'm good.

236
00:16:11,230 --> 00:16:12,277
I’m okay.

237
00:16:13,408 --> 00:16:15,452
<i>Huh? Why are they together?</i>

238
00:16:16,068 --> 00:16:17,611
<i>I thought they weren't on good terms.</i>

239
00:16:19,238 --> 00:16:21,519
<i>Back in New York,</i>

240
00:16:21,544 --> 00:16:24,839
<i>they never spoke to each other</i>
<i>because he thought Kei was a snob.</i>

241
00:16:25,327 --> 00:16:27,663
<i>And Kei never liked</i>
<i>hanging out with him.</i>

242
00:16:28,664 --> 00:16:29,665
<i>What happened?</i>

243
00:16:30,041 --> 00:16:32,488
<i>Was there an apocalypse</i>
<i>and I wasn't informed?</i>

244
00:16:33,294 --> 00:16:34,837
What brings you here?

245
00:16:35,838 --> 00:16:38,632
Um, I just finished my
internship for my MBA.

246
00:16:38,841 --> 00:16:41,177
And I just wanted to visit
the Philippines.

247
00:16:41,594 --> 00:16:44,013
You know, since I left after highschool,

248
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,139
I haven't been back.

249
00:16:45,681 --> 00:16:47,141
What did your mom say?

250
00:16:48,517 --> 00:16:49,727
I don't know.

251
00:16:49,727 --> 00:16:51,228
Let them think what they want.

252
00:16:51,228 --> 00:16:52,646
I'm an adult so,

253
00:16:52,646 --> 00:16:54,815
I can do what I want with my life.

254
00:16:55,357 --> 00:16:57,818
<i>Technically, she's right about that.</i>

255
00:16:57,818 --> 00:17:00,071
<i>But that's not the </i>
<i>answer I was looking for.</i>

256
00:17:00,071 --> 00:17:02,656
<i>I mean...</i>
<i>Why is she here?</i>

257
00:17:03,157 --> 00:17:05,117
<i>As in... here.</i>

258
00:17:05,117 --> 00:17:06,577
<i>At Tripp's home.</i>

259
00:17:06,577 --> 00:17:08,037
<i>With Tripp.</i>

260
00:17:08,524 --> 00:17:10,067
Oh! Speaking of Mom!

261
00:17:10,122 --> 00:17:11,999
She wanted me to give you something.

262
00:17:11,999 --> 00:17:13,751
Wait, it's in the car.

263
00:17:25,763 --> 00:17:26,931
So...

264
00:17:28,140 --> 00:17:29,225
You're back.

265
00:17:32,144 --> 00:17:33,238
Yeah.

266
00:17:33,646 --> 00:17:35,231
Why are you with Kei?

267
00:17:38,984 --> 00:17:39,735
Yeah.

268
00:17:39,826 --> 00:17:41,661
What the hell, Tripp?

269
00:17:44,156 --> 00:17:45,241
What do you mean, what the hell?

270
00:17:45,714 --> 00:17:47,424
You're avoiding me!

271
00:17:51,038 --> 00:17:52,414
That's just in your head, Alys.

272
00:17:54,667 --> 00:17:55,730
See?

273
00:17:56,043 --> 00:17:59,130
You're calling me Alys.
I know something's wrong, Tripp.

274
00:18:02,341 --> 00:18:03,843
That's your name, isn't it?

275
00:18:04,635 --> 00:18:05,803
What's wrong about that?

276
00:18:07,304 --> 00:18:08,180
Tripp!

277
00:18:09,932 --> 00:18:10,808
You're so loud.

278
00:18:11,600 --> 00:18:12,605
Keep it down.

279
00:18:12,893 --> 00:18:14,562
You're still angry with me.

280
00:18:18,149 --> 00:18:19,024
You're overthinking it.

281
00:18:19,692 --> 00:18:21,235
Then talk to me!

282
00:18:21,235 --> 00:18:24,530
For god's sake, talk to me
so I don't overthink.

283
00:18:26,407 --> 00:18:28,534
Because you keep on avoiding me!

284
00:18:31,871 --> 00:18:33,245
Just leave, Alys.

285
00:18:33,831 --> 00:18:34,999
We're just going to fight.

286
00:18:34,999 --> 00:18:36,417
Then let's fight.

287
00:18:36,417 --> 00:18:38,752
Fight me! Do anything!

288
00:18:38,752 --> 00:18:40,838
Just talk to me!

289
00:18:42,423 --> 00:18:43,883
Go home!

290
00:18:54,476 --> 00:18:57,563
Tripp, don't do this to me, please.

291
00:18:59,732 --> 00:19:01,611
- Tripp.
- You said I’m not doing anything, right?

292
00:19:02,484 --> 00:19:04,945
Exactly, you're not doing anything.

293
00:19:04,945 --> 00:19:06,739
Please do something.

294
00:19:07,072 --> 00:19:09,325
Please do something! Anything!

295
00:19:09,658 --> 00:19:10,993
Anything!

296
00:19:11,285 --> 00:19:13,621
This hurts me more than fighting.

297
00:19:14,914 --> 00:19:16,248
Please, don't.

298
00:19:26,634 --> 00:19:29,136
Then give me space, Alys.

299
00:19:30,512 --> 00:19:32,306
We'll talk when I'm better, okay?

300
00:19:34,308 --> 00:19:35,976
What about me?

301
00:19:36,594 --> 00:19:38,804
What if I'm not okay?

302
00:19:40,356 --> 00:19:42,900
Did you consider how I might feel?

303
00:19:43,984 --> 00:19:45,319
How about me?

304
00:19:46,153 --> 00:19:47,863
Did you think about me?

305
00:19:49,240 --> 00:19:50,157
You never did.

306
00:19:51,867 --> 00:19:53,369
I chose you.

307
00:19:53,953 --> 00:19:55,454
I chose you, Tripp.

308
00:19:55,454 --> 00:19:56,956
I chose you!

309
00:19:57,873 --> 00:20:01,377
But here you are acting
such a fucking asshole.

310
00:20:02,586 --> 00:20:03,963
You chose me?

311
00:20:05,381 --> 00:20:06,799
Me? You chose me?

312
00:20:08,175 --> 00:20:09,593
You never chose me!

313
00:20:11,887 --> 00:20:13,472
I was nothing but an option.

314
00:20:16,225 --> 00:20:17,478
Because Drake left you.

315
00:20:19,061 --> 00:20:20,187
So how about Tripp instead.

316
00:20:22,106 --> 00:20:23,393
That's how it was, right?

317
00:20:25,192 --> 00:20:26,318
Ahh...

318
00:20:26,902 --> 00:20:28,070
I’ll just choose Tripp.

319
00:20:28,862 --> 00:20:29,822
He's the one who's around.

320
00:20:30,990 --> 00:20:31,949
He's close.

321
00:20:35,035 --> 00:20:36,578
Did you think that
would make me happy?

322
00:20:39,707 --> 00:20:41,417
It fucked me up, Alys.

323
00:20:43,002 --> 00:20:44,712
It fucked me up real bad.

324
00:21:12,948 --> 00:21:15,200
Let's party!

325
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,244
- Let's go!
- Hee hee!

326
00:21:17,487 --> 00:21:20,581
Come on! Let's get drunk!

327
00:21:22,708 --> 00:21:25,169
Come on, let's go!

328
00:21:27,504 --> 00:21:28,714
Why are you crying?

329
00:21:29,735 --> 00:21:30,945
Is it Drake again?

330
00:21:31,526 --> 00:21:32,986
I swear, if I see him again—

331
00:21:33,335 --> 00:21:34,503
Alys.

332
00:21:35,637 --> 00:21:36,680
It's gonna be okay.

333
00:21:37,931 --> 00:21:39,224
Did Tripp argue with you again?

334
00:21:40,142 --> 00:21:41,065
What?

335
00:21:41,268 --> 00:21:42,269
Why Tripp?

336
00:21:43,103 --> 00:21:44,271
He's her boyfriend, right?

337
00:21:45,105 --> 00:21:46,440
Why would he make her cry?

338
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:48,108
No more questions for now.

339
00:21:49,193 --> 00:21:50,152
Alys...

340
00:21:51,612 --> 00:21:52,738
Alys, calm down.

341
00:21:53,655 --> 00:21:54,573
Calm down.

342
00:21:54,656 --> 00:21:56,784
- Alys, Alys...
- It’s okay, Alys.

343
00:21:56,784 --> 00:21:58,706
Calm down, stop crying.

344
00:21:58,952 --> 00:21:59,995
Stop crying.

345
00:22:43,174 --> 00:22:44,721
Alys!

346
00:22:45,416 --> 00:22:47,252
Honey, are you ready?

347
00:22:53,215 --> 00:22:55,843
I know you're not in
your best mood right now.

348
00:22:56,343 --> 00:22:59,888
But maybe this party can
take your mind off things.

349
00:23:00,722 --> 00:23:01,807
Alright?

350
00:23:02,349 --> 00:23:03,267
Cheer up!

351
00:23:03,475 --> 00:23:05,310
You're wasting your beauty!

352
00:23:05,727 --> 00:23:06,728
Okay?

353
00:23:06,979 --> 00:23:08,522
Alright, I'll be downstairs.

354
00:23:08,522 --> 00:23:09,940
Don't take too long.

355
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:11,442
Okay, Mommy. I'll be right down.

356
00:23:11,442 --> 00:23:12,432
Okay!

357
00:23:16,822 --> 00:23:18,699
<i>At least my family's okay.</i>

358
00:23:19,283 --> 00:23:22,119
<i>Even if everything else is broken.</i>

359
00:23:24,663 --> 00:23:26,290
It's okay, Alys.

360
00:23:28,500 --> 00:23:29,518
You're okay.

361
00:23:30,127 --> 00:23:32,171
Alys, let's go!

362
00:23:32,754 --> 00:23:34,381
Coming!

363
00:23:41,930 --> 00:23:44,725
Hon, remember about the
eye care foundation?

364
00:23:44,725 --> 00:23:47,561
You know what?
Susan donated like 500,000.

365
00:23:47,811 --> 00:23:49,563
We probably should donate.

366
00:23:49,563 --> 00:23:50,814
- What do you think?
- I don’t feel like going.

367
00:23:50,814 --> 00:23:52,107
We'll talk about it later.

368
00:23:52,107 --> 00:23:53,233
So, kids?

369
00:23:53,233 --> 00:23:54,902
Enjoy yourselves, okay?

370
00:23:54,902 --> 00:23:57,029
Go ahead, alright?

371
00:23:57,571 --> 00:23:59,364
Oh, hi, Mr. Lim!

372
00:24:00,748 --> 00:24:02,866
I'm glad you decided
to get out of the house.

373
00:24:02,891 --> 00:24:04,059
It has been days.

374
00:24:04,238 --> 00:24:05,345
You know what, Dane?

375
00:24:05,370 --> 00:24:08,499
If it wasn't required to bring your
family I wouldn't have attended.

376
00:24:09,541 --> 00:24:10,916
Well, we're here.

377
00:24:11,168 --> 00:24:13,003
Let's just make the most out of it.

378
00:24:13,955 --> 00:24:15,839
Hey, where are you going, Dane?

379
00:24:15,839 --> 00:24:17,299
- I'm leaving.
- You're leaving me too?

380
00:24:19,801 --> 00:24:21,261
Such a weirdo.

381
00:24:24,515 --> 00:24:25,974
Suck it up, Alys.

382
00:24:26,350 --> 00:24:27,976
You can do this. Let's go.

383
00:24:28,393 --> 00:24:30,103
Dane, wait up!

384
00:24:31,647 --> 00:24:32,981
Where is he?

385
00:24:35,526 --> 00:24:36,860
Oh my god, I'm so—

386
00:24:37,694 --> 00:24:38,487
I'm sorry.

387
00:24:39,821 --> 00:24:42,491
Alys! You little witch!

388
00:24:42,491 --> 00:24:43,700
Let's go, Fier.

389
00:24:44,451 --> 00:24:45,577
I hate you, you know.

390
00:24:45,602 --> 00:24:46,728
Let's go.

391
00:24:48,163 --> 00:24:49,748
You broke up with him,

392
00:24:49,748 --> 00:24:51,416
but I still can't get him from you.

393
00:24:51,416 --> 00:24:53,252
I'm sorry, Alys. She's just drunk.

394
00:24:54,169 --> 00:24:56,380
You... horrible person.

395
00:24:57,005 --> 00:24:57,714
Horrible person!

396
00:24:57,714 --> 00:24:58,465
Enough!

397
00:24:59,049 --> 00:25:00,010
No!

398
00:25:00,342 --> 00:25:01,343
You don't understand!

399
00:25:01,677 --> 00:25:02,761
Even though you're a horrible person,

400
00:25:02,761 --> 00:25:04,304
I can't get him from you!

401
00:25:04,304 --> 00:25:05,239
Let's go, Fier.

402
00:25:05,264 --> 00:25:06,890
I'm not done with you yet!

403
00:25:06,890 --> 00:25:09,017
You are a horrible person!

404
00:25:09,017 --> 00:25:11,436
You're a witch! You're horrible!

405
00:25:11,645 --> 00:25:12,688
Horrible!

406
00:25:13,855 --> 00:25:15,357
Horrible is a bit much.

407
00:25:18,277 --> 00:25:22,281
<i>They said it was a </i>
<i>miracle that I survived.</i>

408
00:25:22,656 --> 00:25:24,992
<i>Thanks to all the saints </i>
<i>my mom cursed at, </i>

409
00:25:24,992 --> 00:25:27,327
<i>and to the healing potion she </i>
<i>got all the way from Siquijor.</i>

410
00:25:28,787 --> 00:25:30,789
- Alys!
- Hmm?

411
00:25:31,707 --> 00:25:34,001
Aren't you supposed to be
at your work today?

412
00:25:35,335 --> 00:25:37,796
They can manage by themselves.
They're grown ups.

413
00:25:38,797 --> 00:25:40,257
Alys.

414
00:25:40,257 --> 00:25:42,384
That's your business
we're talking about.

415
00:25:42,785 --> 00:25:45,079
That cupcake shop is
your baby, remember?

416
00:25:45,178 --> 00:25:46,065
I know!

417
00:25:47,264 --> 00:25:48,390
They'll manage.

418
00:25:48,390 --> 00:25:49,600
- Dear God.
- Relax.

419
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,350
That's it!

420
00:25:50,434 --> 00:25:51,560
This is getting out of hand.

421
00:25:51,685 --> 00:25:53,312
Enough with the sulking!

422
00:25:53,592 --> 00:25:54,593
Mom, I—

423
00:25:54,618 --> 00:25:55,577
You know what?

424
00:25:55,981 --> 00:25:59,026
You've locked yourself in this
house since the office party.

425
00:25:59,234 --> 00:26:00,902
You need to get out of the house!

426
00:26:01,051 --> 00:26:02,469
You know what?
You're going with us later.

427
00:26:04,156 --> 00:26:05,449
That's not gonna work.

428
00:26:05,657 --> 00:26:07,951
I've had enough of
your sighs and silence.

429
00:26:07,951 --> 00:26:08,952
And you're going.

430
00:26:11,204 --> 00:26:12,014
Where?

431
00:26:12,039 --> 00:26:12,998
A fundraiser event.

432
00:26:13,790 --> 00:26:15,167
Oh come on, Mom.

433
00:26:15,375 --> 00:26:16,376
God, Alys!

434
00:26:16,376 --> 00:26:18,128
Even if you throw a fit,

435
00:26:18,128 --> 00:26:19,521
you're going with us, okay?

436
00:26:19,546 --> 00:26:20,672
Mom!

437
00:26:20,672 --> 00:26:21,340
You're going!

438
00:26:21,340 --> 00:26:22,107
Mommy!

439
00:26:22,132 --> 00:26:22,799
No!

440
00:26:22,799 --> 00:26:25,260
Please stop with bringing
me to your work functions!

441
00:26:25,260 --> 00:26:26,970
Have mercy!

442
00:26:26,970 --> 00:26:28,805
Not working, Alys, okay?

443
00:26:28,805 --> 00:26:30,349
So pick up a nice dress.

444
00:26:30,349 --> 00:26:32,291
I'll have Nanny pick you up, okay?

445
00:26:32,517 --> 00:26:34,061
Alright, see you later!

446
00:26:38,023 --> 00:26:39,486
Mom!

447
00:26:41,902 --> 00:26:43,604
Not even a message.

448
00:26:43,904 --> 00:26:45,989
Nothing from him on social media!

449
00:26:45,989 --> 00:26:49,034
Well, he did ask for space, right?

450
00:26:51,161 --> 00:26:52,579
Yeah, right.

451
00:26:54,665 --> 00:26:55,999
We're just on a break,

452
00:26:55,999 --> 00:26:57,125
not done.

453
00:26:58,460 --> 00:26:59,670
Whatever you guys say.

454
00:27:00,295 --> 00:27:01,004
Wait,

455
00:27:01,588 --> 00:27:04,216
is Tripp doing photography again?

456
00:27:06,009 --> 00:27:09,638
Back in New York, he kept
pushing me to be his model.

457
00:27:10,013 --> 00:27:11,156
Aya?

458
00:27:11,181 --> 00:27:12,432
I need you!

459
00:27:12,724 --> 00:27:13,850
Hang on, Bestie.

460
00:27:13,850 --> 00:27:15,686
Your mom just came in.

461
00:27:16,061 --> 00:27:19,106
I need to present our
designs for our client.

462
00:27:19,106 --> 00:27:22,025
I don't want to get yelled at again.

463
00:27:22,275 --> 00:27:23,527
Okay, good luck.

464
00:27:23,527 --> 00:27:25,862
I told you working there is a bad idea.

465
00:27:25,862 --> 00:27:27,948
My mom is such a terror boss.

466
00:27:28,490 --> 00:27:30,829
- At least, I'm learning.
- Aya!

467
00:27:30,867 --> 00:27:32,369
Yes, Auntie! Coming!

468
00:27:32,369 --> 00:27:34,621
- Bye, Bestie. Have to go.
<i>- Okay, bestie. Bye!</i>

469
00:27:46,883 --> 00:27:47,968
Is this Kei?!

470
00:27:48,927 --> 00:27:50,011
No way.

471
00:27:52,389 --> 00:27:53,849
She'd never betray me.

472
00:27:55,142 --> 00:27:58,353
Kei's the closest thing I
have to a sister, next to Aya.

473
00:28:02,315 --> 00:28:04,025
No...

474
00:28:04,943 --> 00:28:07,070
No, she'll never hurt me.

475
00:28:07,946 --> 00:28:09,489
<i>Mommy's right.</i>

476
00:28:09,489 --> 00:28:13,118
<i>I've been wallowing in self-pity,</i>
<i>that I forgot how to live.</i>

477
00:28:13,827 --> 00:28:16,243
<i>There's more to life</i>
<i>than this mess I'm in.</i>

478
00:28:16,747 --> 00:28:20,001
<i>I need to see that my life</i>
<i>is actually still worth living.</i>

479
00:28:20,459 --> 00:28:23,920
<i>That the people around me</i>
<i>are still worth trusting.</i>

480
00:28:24,880 --> 00:28:27,424
I need to breathe. Breathe, Alys.

481
00:28:28,133 --> 00:28:29,415
Get yourself ready.

482
00:28:34,639 --> 00:28:35,595
Mommy!

483
00:28:35,974 --> 00:28:37,618
Are you there in the venue?

484
00:28:37,934 --> 00:28:39,144
<i>Yes, Honey.</i>

485
00:28:39,770 --> 00:28:42,606
Okay, I'm also here in the lobby.
I'll see you there.

486
00:28:42,606 --> 00:28:44,107
<i>Alright, see you!</i>

487
00:28:44,107 --> 00:28:45,150
Okay, bye!

488
00:28:48,987 --> 00:28:50,030
<i>Where you at?</i>

489
00:28:50,030 --> 00:28:51,239
<i>Fundraising event?</i>

490
00:28:51,239 --> 00:28:52,449
<i>Are you gonna be there?</i>

491
00:28:53,366 --> 00:28:55,952
<i>Kei isn't doing anything wrong,</i>

492
00:28:55,952 --> 00:28:56,536
<i>Yet...</i>

493
00:28:56,536 --> 00:28:59,956
<i>something within me makes</i>
<i>me start to hate her.</i>

494
00:28:59,956 --> 00:29:01,917
<i>It's the worst feeling in the world</i>

495
00:29:01,917 --> 00:29:06,087
<i>when you start to doubt</i>
<i>your own bestfriend.</i>

496
00:29:07,221 --> 00:29:10,474
I need a resolve.
It can't always be like this.

497
00:29:13,428 --> 00:29:15,597
Yeah! See you!

498
00:29:18,016 --> 00:29:19,228
<i>See you, Kei.</i>

499
00:29:19,851 --> 00:29:21,686
<i>And talk to you, as well.</i>

500
00:29:22,604 --> 00:29:24,907
<i>I can't keep living like this.</i>

501
00:29:25,440 --> 00:29:27,071
<i>All this paranoia,</i>

502
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:29,361
<i>will be the death of me.</i>

503
00:29:32,030 --> 00:29:33,782
You know what?
Just enjoy the night.

504
00:29:34,407 --> 00:29:36,660
I'll try, Dad.
But I don't even know where<i>—</i>

505
00:29:36,660 --> 00:29:38,032
- Mr. Guzman
- It’s gonna be fun.

506
00:29:38,620 --> 00:29:39,871
Mr. Montreal!

507
00:29:40,121 --> 00:29:40,806
How are you?

508
00:29:40,831 --> 00:29:43,124
I'm good.
Meet my daughter, Alys.

509
00:29:43,583 --> 00:29:44,584
Hi, Alys.

510
00:29:44,709 --> 00:29:45,752
Oh, nice to meet you, sir.

511
00:29:45,752 --> 00:29:47,587
Alys, you remember Mr. Montreal, right?

512
00:29:47,754 --> 00:29:49,047
One of our business partners.

513
00:29:49,047 --> 00:29:50,064
Yes, I do, Dad.

514
00:29:50,382 --> 00:29:51,216
By the way,

515
00:29:52,259 --> 00:29:53,837
I want you to meet my daughter.

516
00:29:54,010 --> 00:29:55,428
This is Natalia.

517
00:29:55,929 --> 00:29:57,597
Hi, Natalia!

518
00:29:58,473 --> 00:29:59,641
Sorry, she's a bit shy.

519
00:30:01,226 --> 00:30:02,644
So, Alys...

520
00:30:02,644 --> 00:30:03,979
you good on your own?

521
00:30:03,979 --> 00:30:05,063
Yes, Dad. I'll manage.

522
00:30:05,063 --> 00:30:06,147
Alright.

523
00:30:06,648 --> 00:30:07,290
Hi, Natalia!

524
00:30:07,315 --> 00:30:08,525
- Nice seeing you.
- Nice seeing you.

525
00:30:17,192 --> 00:30:18,564
Is Kei here?

526
00:30:28,432 --> 00:30:30,434
Thank god!
Someone I actually know.

527
00:30:30,714 --> 00:30:32,007
What happened to you?

528
00:30:33,550 --> 00:30:35,552
Wow, someone’s thirsty.

529
00:30:37,053 --> 00:30:39,389
Goodness, thank God you're here!

530
00:30:39,973 --> 00:30:41,975
Mommy couldn't make it so

531
00:30:41,975 --> 00:30:44,644
I was sent here to be her proxy.

532
00:30:45,687 --> 00:30:47,480
Are you with your family?

533
00:30:47,898 --> 00:30:49,333
What about you?

534
00:30:51,026 --> 00:30:52,360
Did you come alone?

535
00:30:54,029 --> 00:30:55,780
It was a short notice.

536
00:30:55,780 --> 00:30:57,407
I'm glad you're here.

537
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:01,244
<i>How did I ever doubt her?</i>

538
00:31:02,203 --> 00:31:04,164
<i>I know she'll never hurt me.</i>

539
00:31:07,675 --> 00:31:08,843
I need more wine!

540
00:31:09,085 --> 00:31:10,170
Looks like it.

541
00:31:10,170 --> 00:31:11,379
Let's go.

542
00:31:14,716 --> 00:31:16,843
- Whatever, Alys.
- About to start singing?

543
00:31:17,218 --> 00:31:19,012
- Hey!
- I'm kidding.

544
00:31:19,012 --> 00:31:20,263
Hello, ladies!

545
00:31:20,430 --> 00:31:21,765
- Hi, Uncle!
- Hi, Kei.

546
00:31:21,765 --> 00:31:22,849
Nice to see you.

547
00:31:23,433 --> 00:31:24,225
Dear...

548
00:31:24,225 --> 00:31:26,716
you can only spend up
to one million tonight, okay?

549
00:31:27,812 --> 00:31:28,563
Okay, Dad!

550
00:31:28,563 --> 00:31:30,523
As if I plan on bidding tonight.

551
00:31:30,523 --> 00:31:31,983
I'm just saying!

552
00:31:32,008 --> 00:31:33,654
So I'll just go to the front, okay?

553
00:31:33,818 --> 00:31:34,527
Go ahead, Dad.

554
00:31:34,527 --> 00:31:35,725
You guys enjoy yourselves.

555
00:31:35,750 --> 00:31:36,717
Thank you, Dad.

556
00:31:42,452 --> 00:31:43,453
So...

557
00:31:45,288 --> 00:31:46,456
have you seen Tripp?

558
00:31:49,209 --> 00:31:50,543
Did you two fight?

559
00:31:51,753 --> 00:31:53,338
I saw him recently.

560
00:31:54,422 --> 00:31:56,758
You guys should talk it out.

561
00:31:57,759 --> 00:31:59,678
Like it or not...

562
00:32:00,929 --> 00:32:03,473
the problem won't go away
unless you two talk about it.

563
00:32:04,140 --> 00:32:05,517
You're just dragging it out.

564
00:32:07,978 --> 00:32:09,688
I really want to talk to him.

565
00:32:09,688 --> 00:32:11,314
I'm just waiting for him.

566
00:32:12,524 --> 00:32:15,485
Ladies and gentlemen,
thank you for your patience.

567
00:32:15,485 --> 00:32:18,446
Kindly settle down and take your seats.

568
00:32:21,491 --> 00:32:23,868
Cut the self-pity, Perez!

569
00:32:25,120 --> 00:32:28,707
You know Tripp followed
you around like a dog once.

570
00:32:28,957 --> 00:32:31,668
You're worth it, okay?

571
00:32:32,377 --> 00:32:33,962
Never forget that.

572
00:32:37,549 --> 00:32:39,551
I really missed you, Kei.

573
00:32:40,411 --> 00:32:41,787
I missed you, too.

574
00:32:43,596 --> 00:32:47,851
All of our proceeds from tonight’s program
will go directly to DAHON.

575
00:32:47,851 --> 00:32:52,856
A Dedicated Alliance for
Helping and Healing Our Nature.

576
00:32:53,064 --> 00:32:55,025
Let's give it up for DAHON, everybody.

577
00:32:55,984 --> 00:32:57,360
Up for grabs first,

578
00:32:57,360 --> 00:33:00,280
is a 90-year old bottle of wine courtesy

579
00:33:00,280 --> 00:33:03,408
of the very generous Sandoval family.

580
00:33:03,408 --> 00:33:07,245
Made by the best wine
makers in all of France.

581
00:33:07,912 --> 00:33:09,831
My god, Alys.

582
00:33:10,248 --> 00:33:12,375
Ever since we were in New York,

583
00:33:13,168 --> 00:33:15,128
when it comes to love,

584
00:33:15,128 --> 00:33:17,672
you never failed to be stupid.

585
00:33:18,506 --> 00:33:19,174
Ouch!

586
00:33:19,174 --> 00:33:21,009
Isn't stupid a bit much?

587
00:33:21,009 --> 00:33:23,595
Can't I just be someone
who gives it my all?

588
00:33:23,595 --> 00:33:24,220
And...

589
00:33:25,221 --> 00:33:26,723
a hopeless romantic.

590
00:33:26,723 --> 00:33:28,933
- A little?
- Just a little bit.

591
00:33:29,167 --> 00:33:31,478
A little that's also kind of a lot.

592
00:33:31,478 --> 00:33:33,146
Wow!

593
00:33:33,146 --> 00:33:34,689
Whatever, Alys.

594
00:33:34,689 --> 00:33:36,066
Let’s stick with that.

595
00:33:37,484 --> 00:33:38,651
Oh!

596
00:33:39,652 --> 00:33:40,987
Hang on, it's Mommy.

597
00:33:40,987 --> 00:33:42,447
I need to take this.

598
00:33:43,615 --> 00:33:47,410
You may now start the
bidding at 100,000 pesos.

599
00:33:47,410 --> 00:33:50,163
Anybody have a 100,000?
Anybody interested?

600
00:33:50,163 --> 00:33:53,583
Yes, Mr. Santos how about
we bump it to a 115,000 pesos?

601
00:33:53,583 --> 00:33:57,128
Yes, Mrs. Alivar! 115,000?

602
00:33:57,128 --> 00:34:00,173
To the gentleman
in the black tie. 115,000!

603
00:34:00,231 --> 00:34:03,276
How about we
bump it to 120,000?

604
00:34:03,301 --> 00:34:04,677
<i>Where is Kei?</i>

605
00:34:04,928 --> 00:34:06,805
Did she forget to
come back for me?

606
00:34:07,972 --> 00:34:09,682
Gosh, everyone seems to do so.

607
00:34:12,143 --> 00:34:13,853
Where did she go?

608
00:34:15,021 --> 00:34:19,609
Mrs. Alivar, sold!
For 200,000 pesos!

609
00:34:21,903 --> 00:34:25,156
<i>And now, for our next auction item.</i>

610
00:34:25,156 --> 00:34:27,951
<i>An original painting by </i>
<i>Alejandro Perin.</i>

611
00:34:27,951 --> 00:34:31,412
<i>The bidding starts at 250,000.</i>

612
00:34:31,955 --> 00:34:33,373
<i>Thank you, Ma’am!</i>

613
00:34:33,373 --> 00:34:35,500
<i>Do I hear 300,000?</i>

614
00:34:35,901 --> 00:34:39,154
It's like I'm talking to the
slowest person in the world!

615
00:34:40,088 --> 00:34:42,006
You weren't answering my calls!

616
00:34:42,006 --> 00:34:43,297
What was I gonna do?

617
00:34:43,675 --> 00:34:44,926
My god, Tripp!

618
00:34:45,301 --> 00:34:46,886
We can't be together!

619
00:34:47,720 --> 00:34:48,680
There is no us!

620
00:34:48,680 --> 00:34:50,390
Are you dumb? Are you insane?

621
00:34:50,598 --> 00:34:51,808
Maybe both!

622
00:34:52,225 --> 00:34:53,434
Kei, don’t do—

623
00:34:54,102 --> 00:34:55,478
Get it together, Tripp!

624
00:34:57,063 --> 00:34:59,566
You're still with Alys! My best friend!

625
00:35:00,108 --> 00:35:02,152
How many times do
I have to repeat that?

626
00:35:02,986 --> 00:35:04,195
My god!

627
00:35:04,195 --> 00:35:05,655
You're giving me a headache!

628
00:35:06,489 --> 00:35:08,867
I don't care about you,
Tripp Marco Palma!

629
00:35:10,876 --> 00:35:14,838
Dating my friend's ex, is not
something I'm comfortable with!

630
00:35:15,748 --> 00:35:17,167
Not now,

631
00:35:17,167 --> 00:35:18,459
not ever!

632
00:35:18,459 --> 00:35:20,879
So please, stop this already!

633
00:35:21,713 --> 00:35:24,132
You have to fix things with Alys!

634
00:35:24,672 --> 00:35:26,491
She's a good person.

635
00:35:26,759 --> 00:35:29,053
You should be grateful she stuck by you!

636
00:35:29,971 --> 00:35:31,222
If it were me,

637
00:35:32,307 --> 00:35:34,225
I'd have left you a long time ago!

638
00:35:35,852 --> 00:35:37,145
So, leave.

639
00:35:37,770 --> 00:35:39,480
Before she sees us.

640
00:35:39,939 --> 00:35:41,232
Never do this again, okay?

641
00:35:42,150 --> 00:35:43,193
Please!

642
00:36:23,233 --> 00:36:26,444
<i>I'm going home. Sorry for ditching.</i>

643
00:36:26,444 --> 00:36:28,029
<i>Rain check?</i>

644
00:36:32,932 --> 00:36:34,517
Calm down, Alys.

645
00:36:36,246 --> 00:36:37,705
Everything will make sense in time.

646
00:36:37,705 --> 00:36:38,873
You're okay.

647
00:36:39,791 --> 00:36:40,917
You're okay.

648
00:37:17,704 --> 00:37:18,790
Tripp...

649
00:37:20,707 --> 00:37:22,282
Can we talk?

650
00:37:27,213 --> 00:37:29,966
I know you heard
Kei and I talking, Alys.

651
00:37:31,551 --> 00:37:32,969
What are you, a masochist?

652
00:37:34,887 --> 00:37:35,722
Tripp...

653
00:37:36,723 --> 00:37:38,391
I thought we were just taking a break?

654
00:37:38,850 --> 00:37:40,685
We never broke up, right?

655
00:37:49,444 --> 00:37:50,532
Okay, Alys.

656
00:37:52,071 --> 00:37:53,114
Let's break up.

657
00:37:54,532 --> 00:37:55,825
Are you being serious, Tripp?

658
00:38:00,288 --> 00:38:01,414
I refuse, Tripp.

659
00:38:01,873 --> 00:38:03,374
I will not let you.

660
00:38:04,050 --> 00:38:05,384
You’re not leaving me.

661
00:38:05,960 --> 00:38:07,295
You're not leaving me, Tripp!

662
00:38:07,587 --> 00:38:08,629
Listen.

663
00:38:10,131 --> 00:38:11,257
There's nothing left.

664
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:13,926
I'm done.

665
00:38:15,094 --> 00:38:16,110
Let's end this.

666
00:38:17,096 --> 00:38:17,972
I'm tired.

667
00:38:19,474 --> 00:38:22,477
You're just saying that!
You're not even trying!

668
00:38:26,105 --> 00:38:27,985
Do you even hear yourself, Alys?

669
00:38:29,650 --> 00:38:31,486
All these years, Alys.

670
00:38:32,987 --> 00:38:34,906
The only thing I've done is try.

671
00:38:37,283 --> 00:38:38,860
Do you know where we went wrong?

672
00:38:42,497 --> 00:38:44,207
It's how you acknowledge me.

673
00:38:44,499 --> 00:38:46,167
Even for just one day.

674
00:38:46,167 --> 00:38:48,821
One day is all I ask,
that you get to acknowledge

675
00:38:49,295 --> 00:38:51,589
and see my efforts,
but it just never happened.

676
00:38:52,465 --> 00:38:53,591
You never saw it.

677
00:38:56,469 --> 00:38:57,845
I'm done, Zy.

678
00:38:58,930 --> 00:39:00,306
So, please...

679
00:39:01,719 --> 00:39:03,095
stop being selfish.

680
00:39:04,977 --> 00:39:06,354
All I want

681
00:39:07,063 --> 00:39:08,439
is a life without you.

682
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:13,087
A life that isn't focused around you.

683
00:39:13,319 --> 00:39:14,570
That's all I want.

684
00:39:15,530 --> 00:39:17,031
Please let me live my life.

685
00:39:18,455 --> 00:39:20,415
Don't you love me anymore?

686
00:39:30,044 --> 00:39:31,110
I still do.

687
00:39:36,092 --> 00:39:38,761
Then why are you hurting me?

688
00:39:48,479 --> 00:39:50,930
Because you never loved me
the way I wanted you to, Perez.

689
00:39:55,528 --> 00:39:57,071
All of my life,

690
00:39:58,030 --> 00:39:59,282
I had to share with Drake.

691
00:39:59,282 --> 00:40:00,116
You know that.

692
00:40:01,742 --> 00:40:03,868
That's why, when it comes to women,

693
00:40:04,120 --> 00:40:05,493
I don’t want to have to share too.

694
00:40:07,490 --> 00:40:09,876
But I chose you.

695
00:40:12,503 --> 00:40:14,464
No, you didn't, Alys.

696
00:40:16,110 --> 00:40:17,300
You never did.

697
00:40:18,843 --> 00:40:20,052
It was Drake.

698
00:40:21,971 --> 00:40:23,181
- It always has been.
- That’s not true.

699
00:40:23,389 --> 00:40:24,390
That’s not true.

700
00:40:25,349 --> 00:40:26,516
It was Drake

701
00:40:26,726 --> 00:40:28,102
and it always will be.

702
00:40:29,395 --> 00:40:30,774
I've accepted that, Alys.

703
00:40:34,233 --> 00:40:35,485
Come on, Tripp.

704
00:40:37,195 --> 00:40:38,446
Tripp...

705
00:40:40,448 --> 00:40:41,449
Don't worry.

706
00:40:43,242 --> 00:40:44,452
I promise you,

707
00:40:45,719 --> 00:40:46,929
go after Drake first.

708
00:40:48,915 --> 00:40:50,458
And if it doesn’t work out,

709
00:40:52,752 --> 00:40:54,295
I'll come running back to you.

710
00:40:57,173 --> 00:40:58,966
Why do you have to be such a jerk?

711
00:41:01,427 --> 00:41:03,971
You and I both know
what'll happen if I won’t be.

712
00:41:06,432 --> 00:41:08,434
I'm just gonna crawl
myself back to you.

713
00:41:12,021 --> 00:41:13,856
I'm pathetic without you, Perez.

714
00:41:17,193 --> 00:41:19,487
Then, let's be pathetic together.

715
00:41:20,863 --> 00:41:24,325
You know how happy
I am when I'm with you.

716
00:41:27,036 --> 00:41:29,288
Tripp, please. Don't leave me.

717
00:41:33,918 --> 00:41:36,879
Tripp, please don't leave me.

718
00:41:36,904 --> 00:41:41,075
Please, don't leave me.

719
00:41:41,217 --> 00:41:43,302
Don't leave me, Tripp.

720
00:41:44,720 --> 00:41:47,751
- Perez, Perez!
- Don't leave me.

721
00:41:48,724 --> 00:41:52,061
What we need to try,
is to end things for real.

722
00:41:54,744 --> 00:41:56,162
Don't worry.

723
00:41:57,316 --> 00:41:58,734
I promise you my name.

724
00:42:01,279 --> 00:42:02,863
If Drake doesn't come back to you,

725
00:42:05,256 --> 00:42:06,841
then I'll marry you.

726
00:42:09,829 --> 00:42:10,955
But for now...

727
00:42:12,832 --> 00:42:13,958
that's enough, Zy.

728
00:42:15,251 --> 00:42:16,961
Don't leave me.

729
00:42:19,797 --> 00:42:21,507
This is hard for me, too.

730
00:42:38,190 --> 00:42:39,900
You're my soulmate.

731
00:42:43,195 --> 00:42:45,524
Sometimes soulmates
don't end up with each other.

732
00:42:48,367 --> 00:42:49,619
I'm sorry, Zy.

733
00:43:00,046 --> 00:43:04,383
Tripp, please don't leave me.

734
00:43:14,310 --> 00:43:15,297
Friends?

735
00:43:17,146 --> 00:43:19,492
You'll marry me someday, Tripp.

736
00:43:19,857 --> 00:43:21,692
You'll marry me.

737
00:43:24,654 --> 00:43:26,697
<i>I am not even sure anymore.</i>

738
00:43:28,240 --> 00:43:29,437
Tripp, no!

739
00:44:08,364 --> 00:44:09,989
I'm setting you free.

740
00:44:11,534 --> 00:44:13,317
So, please let me go as well.

741
00:44:14,662 --> 00:44:16,956
We should let go of each other.

742
00:44:18,999 --> 00:44:20,793
Take care of my cousin.

743
00:44:27,049 --> 00:44:28,356
Best wishes.

744
00:44:28,843 --> 00:44:29,958
[in French] Only you.

745
00:45:07,548 --> 00:45:09,454
<i>I'm sorry, Alys.</i>

746
00:45:10,735 --> 00:45:12,493
<i>I have to do this.</i>

747
00:45:13,846 --> 00:45:15,157
<i>I love you.</i>

748
00:45:15,639 --> 00:45:19,560
<i>I guess I love you more </i>
<i>than I ever did.</i>

749
00:45:20,978 --> 00:45:23,481
<i>And I know what I did hurt you.</i>

750
00:45:24,273 --> 00:45:28,110
<i>But if I stay, I'll only confuse you.</i>

751
00:45:31,447 --> 00:45:33,449
<i>I want to reach out to you.</i>

752
00:45:33,449 --> 00:45:38,204
<i>I want to hold you close </i>
<i>and tell you that I want us back.</i>

753
00:45:38,913 --> 00:45:42,750
<i>But you already turned me down </i>
<i>when you didn't show up for our wedding.</i>

754
00:45:43,586 --> 00:45:45,344
<i>That broke my heart, Alys.</i>

755
00:45:45,711 --> 00:45:49,477
<i>Nothing hurts more than not being </i>
<i>chosen by the person you love so deeply.</i>

756
00:45:51,756 --> 00:45:52,937
<i>If we're really meant to be,</i>

757
00:45:53,260 --> 00:45:57,157
<i>I know we'll always find </i>
<i>our way back to each other.</i>

758
00:45:58,098 --> 00:46:00,157
<i>Thank you for everything, my Noob.</i>

759
00:46:00,518 --> 00:46:03,229
<i>I'll wait for you until the very end.</i>

760
00:46:35,135 --> 00:46:37,471
<i>Since the day I met you, Alys,</i>

761
00:46:38,472 --> 00:46:42,685
<i>I did nothing but love you with all I had.</i>

762
00:46:44,282 --> 00:46:46,242
<i>I never ran out of love to give.</i>

763
00:46:47,343 --> 00:46:49,594
<i>Even when I knew deep down,</i>

764
00:46:50,526 --> 00:46:52,361
<i>that I'd always come second.</i>

765
00:46:53,654 --> 00:46:54,821
<i>But now?</i>

766
00:46:56,490 --> 00:46:57,741
<i>It hurts.</i>

767
00:46:58,367 --> 00:46:59,743
<i>It hurts me, Alys.</i>

768
00:47:00,369 --> 00:47:01,745
<i>It hurts me so much.</i>

769
00:47:03,414 --> 00:47:04,790
<i>I love you so much.</i>

770
00:47:05,624 --> 00:47:06,750
<i>That’s why...</i>

771
00:47:07,347 --> 00:47:08,932
<i>I'm setting you free.</i>

772
00:47:10,254 --> 00:47:12,798
<i>This may destroy me but...</i>

773
00:47:13,465 --> 00:47:14,842
<i>I'll do this</i>

774
00:47:15,558 --> 00:47:18,032
<i>because I love you.</i>

775
00:47:19,305 --> 00:47:20,931
<i>I love you, Alys.</i>

776
00:47:22,224 --> 00:47:23,475
<i>I always will.</i>

777
00:47:35,473 --> 00:47:38,726
<i>On the next episode of</i>
<i>Dating Alys Perez.</i>

778
00:47:39,074 --> 00:47:41,035
Auntie said you’re taking a vacation.

779
00:47:41,060 --> 00:47:43,062
Yes, I’m on the way
to Batangas.

780
00:47:46,290 --> 00:47:47,333
Drake?!

781
00:47:47,333 --> 00:47:49,835
Actually Ma'am,
all rooms are occupied.

782
00:47:49,960 --> 00:47:52,463
But the good thing is...

783
00:47:52,463 --> 00:47:56,091
the upper villa is still
available for the two of you!

784
00:47:56,216 --> 00:47:57,968
Enjoy your stay!

785
00:47:57,968 --> 00:48:00,554
Love, love, love!

786
00:48:00,863 --> 00:48:03,699
This place is a perfect place

787
00:48:03,724 --> 00:48:07,811
to relax, enjoy, and be in love.

788
00:48:09,104 --> 00:48:11,065
With the nature, of course.

789
00:48:11,534 --> 00:48:12,477
What the?!

790
00:48:23,243 --> 00:48:25,788
Isn't the sunset so beautiful?

791
00:48:27,873 --> 00:48:29,423
As beautiful as you.
